{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Who establishes the word of His servant.</b> This is the prophet, and the meaning is self-evident. And what is the word of the prophet? That Jerusalem shall be inhabited:" "<b>[shall be inhabited].</b> Derived from ישיבה (settlement), like תורד (Isaiah 14:15)." "<b>and her ruins.</b> The ruins of every single city, or the heh is a sign referring to Jerusalem."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:03.581773755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}